; tests/bml-multiline-def-band.fk — the band for multi-line def bodies on the
; .bml floor lane. Verdict 15.
; PROOF LEVEL: FOURTH-ARM ONLY — the .bml floor is fkwu's own lane (go dies on the .bml prelude, witnessed 2026-09-03); the three
; minimal walkers carry no .bml lowering.
;
; preludes: observe/tests/bml-multiline-def-fixture.bml
;
; The pair shape is the wound shape of 2026-09-02: the form.bml section walker
; dispatched flat statements one LINE at a time while the block walker already
; walked whole quote/paren-aware statements. A def whose call body tore across
; lines lowered to unbalanced text and refused loudly; a def whose if body
; started on the next line bound with the EMPTY expr as its body — it answered
; [] forever with zero diagnostics (observe/preflight-run.fk saw a clean chain)
; while the real body evaluated as a stray top-level statement. Healed in
; fsc-form-bml-lines-recipes-loop: flat statements now walk to their own `;`
; (fsc-bml-stmt-end) and normalize before dispatch, and an empty def body
; refuses loudly in fsc-compile-form-bml-def-recipe — silence never
; impersonates a bound def.
;
; b1 stands on the single-line control def.
; b2 stands on the torn call body — the loud pre-heal mode, now carried.
; b4/b8 stand on the wrapped if body, both branches — the NUMB pre-heal mode:
; before the heal b4/b8 read [] from the def and the band answers 3.

(do
    (defn bmdb-k (cond bit) (if cond bit 0))
    (defn bml-multiline-def-band ()
        (add (add (add
            (bmdb-k (eq (bmd-one-line 41) 42) 1)
            (bmdb-k (eq (bmd-call-lines 41) 42) 2))
            (bmdb-k (eq (bmd-if-lines 0) 0) 4))
            (bmdb-k (eq (bmd-if-lines 5) 1) 8)))
    (bml-multiline-def-band))
